How Typedown thinks about content. Start from the top (the vault) and zoom in to the details.

## Sections

- [Vault](01-vault): the graph, project structure, and configuration
- [Documents](02-documents): nodes in the graph, frontmatter and markdown body
- [Schemas](03-schemas): node types, inheritance, and field definitions
- [Expressions](04-expressions): computed fields, operators, closures, and interpolation
- [References](05-references): edges in the graph, file linking, and traversal
